.TH SIG\-HASH 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.3.3" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
sig\-hash \- Solidity function/event/error selector and topic hash, plus reverse lookup against a file you supply
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
sig\-hash [SIGNATURE...] [\-\-abi FILE] [\-\-lookup HASH \-\-sigs FILE] [\-\-keccak [HEX]]
With no SIGNATURE arguments, signatures are read one per line from stdin.
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Offline, no network, no built\-in signature database. One JSON object per line.
.nf
.RS 2
  sig\-hash 'transfer(address,uint256)'
  sig\-hash 'event Transfer(address indexed from, address indexed to, uint256 value)'
  sig\-hash \-\-lookup 0x5bf6f916 \-\-sigs my\-errors.txt
  echo 0x68656c6c6f | sig\-hash \-\-keccak
.RE
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
  \-\-abi FILE      print selector/topic for every function, event and error in an ABI JSON file
  \-\-lookup HASH   find a 4\-byte selector or 32\-byte topic among the signatures in \-\-sigs (no built\-in database)
  \-\-sigs FILE     ABI JSON, or one signature per line (# comments), used by \-\-lookup
  \-\-keccak [HEX]  keccak256 of hex bytes (argument or stdin)
.fi
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
Offline, no network, no built\-in signature database. One JSON object per line.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Measured on Linux by the EXAMPLES below (scripts/gen\-man.py runs them):
.TP
0
last status ok
.TP
2
last status bad_input
.PP
Not every tool uses the same code for bad input: some exit 1, others exit 2 (docs/FINDINGS.md D1\-14). Always read the last JSON status line. Status and failure codes: docs/REFUSALS.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ sig\-hash 'transfer(address,uint256)'
# exit 0, last status: ok
$ sig\-hash 'not a signature('
# exit 2, last status: bad_input
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
It may open hostile wallet files and handle secrets: run it sealed and offline (./blocktools run; sealed\-run allows it).
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
.SH SEE ALSO
blocktools(7), docs/SECURITY.md, docs/getting\-started.md, recipes/README.md
